### 3.2 Providers and Configuration

| Provider | Rate Control | Quality Parameter | Codec Support | Black-box? |
|----------|-------------|-------------------|---------------|------------|
{% for p in providers | sort(attribute='name') %}| {{ p.name }} | {{ p.rate_control }} | {{ p.quality_param }} | {{ p.codec_support }} | {{ "Yes" if p.blackbox else "No" }} |
{% endfor %}

**Fairness statement:** Each provider was configured to produce the smallest possible file size at a given target quality (VMAF). For providers with quality controls, an interpolation search over each provider's quality parameter finds the setting that hits each VMAF target. For providers without quality controls, the single output represents the provider's best-effort encoding.

**Configurable providers:** For each clip, an interpolation search over each provider's quality parameter finds the setting that hits target VMAF scores ({{ vmaf_targets | join(', ') }}). This produces matched-quality data points for direct comparison.

### 3.3 Quality Measurement

- **VMAF model:** vmaf_v0.6.1neg
- **Evaluation:** Full-video, frame-by-frame (no temporal sampling)
- **Bitrate:** Measured via ffprobe on the actual output file (not provider-reported labels)
- **Metrics extracted per rendition:**
  - VMAF mean, VMAF minimum, VMAF harmonic mean
  - VMAF 1st percentile, VMAF 5th percentile
  - Per-frame VMAF scores (for consistency analysis)
- **Compression ratio:** Input file size ÷ output file size
- **BD-Rate:** Bjontegaard Delta Rate computed between each provider's RD curve and the best-performing provider as reference, using PCHIP interpolation over the overlapping VMAF range

**Why percentiles matter:** A file with VMAF mean 95 but a 1st-percentile of 72 has severe transient quality drops that a viewer will notice. Mean VMAF alone is insufficient for quality assessment.

**Metric chosen for Vidaio:** Vidaio only supports `vmaf_v0.6.1neg` - no other VMAF model, PSNR, SSIM, or other quality metric can be targeted. This dictates the benchmark metric for the entire report, since Vidaio could not be included otherwise. The other providers (AWS MediaConvert, Bitmovin, Brightcove Zencoder) have no such restriction and can be benchmarked against any quality metric.

